  $PROGRAM_NAME ip --external --probe-url https://example.net/ip pppoe1

The ip command never changes network configuration, routes, DNS records,
cron jobs, or files on the router.
EOF
}

show_update_help()
{
	cat <<EOF
Usage:
  $PROGRAM_NAME update --domain-id ID --token-file FILE [options] RECORD

Set the A and/or AAAA records for one Linode DNS record name to the exact IP
address lists given on the command line. Address options may be repeated.
An address family that is not specified is left unchanged.

Required:
      --domain-id ID      Linode domain ID
      --token-file FILE   File containing the API token
  -4, --ipv4 ADDRESS      Desired IPv4 address; may be repeated
  -6, --ipv6 ADDRESS      Desired IPv6 address; may be repeated

Options:
      --clear-ipv4        Delete all A records for RECORD
      --clear-ipv6        Delete all AAAA records for RECORD
      --ttl SECONDS       Record TTL (default: 300)
  -h, --help              Show this help

Examples:
  $PROGRAM_NAME update --domain-id 123 --token-file /root/linode.token -4 192.0.2.10 host
  $PROGRAM_NAME update --domain-id 123 --token-file /root/linode.token -6 2001:db8::10 -6 2001:db8::11 host
  $PROGRAM_NAME update --domain-id 123 --token-file /root/linode.token --clear-ipv6 host

For each specified family, matching records are kept, missing records are
created, and stale or duplicate records are updated or deleted. Same-name
CNAME records are removed when new A or AAAA records are requested. A clear
